// The registers of the bus interface (BIF 5.0) of the Radeon RX 580 (Polaris
// 10) as Linux v6.6 has them. GENERATED by tools/gpu_registers_generate.py
// (do not edit: generate it again; README.md beside it says how a register
// is added) from drivers/gpu/drm/amd/include/asic_reg/bif/bif_5_0_d.h and
// bif/bif_5_0_sh_mask.h, whose sha256 are
//   bif_5_0_d.h       2e8e70894de1edae1b7316570432c81a9e878d376f153d95311ecd808b238ca1
//   bif_5_0_sh_mask.h 2ee6de4fbfd76adf73b985bb2340b385067ac862297eee24357ddc132b2818f2
//
// 15 of the header's 1043 registers, the ones SELECTION names, each with
// every field the header gives it (46 fields). A register is its number as
// Linux and the kernel count it, the dword index of its MMIO word (the
// header's mmNAME without "mm"; a register of an index space keeps the
// header's "ix"). NAME__FIELD is a field's mask, NAME__FIELD__SHIFT its
// lowest bit; an enum is a struct of its values.

